Audit complete. 39 rules sampled across 11 batches. Zero meaning drift found. The transformation is purely structural: unmarked prose → rule-ID-marked, RFC-2119-formalized, single-owner-referenced rules.

```acceptance-report
{
  "criteriaSatisfied": [
    {
      "id": "criterion-1",
      "status": "satisfied",
      "evidence": "Sampled 2+ representative rules per batch across all 11 epic batches (#1147-#1159) plus post-epic follow-ups. Compared pre-epic baseline (8cda46da) against current HEAD for each rule. Verified conditions, guards, exceptions, and modality intact. Found zero meaning drift across 39 sampled rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "criterion-2",
      "status": "satisfied",
      "evidence": "Audit report includes: per-batch before/after excerpts with line-level comparison, a cross-cutting modality verification table mapping all 8 rule families, explicit handling of the one genuine semantic change (internal_tooling_direct_gate addition), and the redundant-text-removal class analysis. All evidence is in the output file."
    }
  ],
  "changedFiles": [
    ".pi-subagents/artifacts/outputs/363fd6c8/tmp/audits/claude-sonnet-4/scope-5-semantic-drift.md"
  ],
  "testsAddedOrUpdated": [],
  "commandsRun": [
    {
      "command": "git diff --stat 8cda46da..HEAD -- skills/docs/ skills/ docs/ agents/ commands/",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "38 files changed, +1009/-760 lines across the epic"
    },
    {
      "command": "git diff per-batch ranges (11 ranges)",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "Sampled 2-3 representative rules from each batch; all diffs confirmed mechanical rewrites with zero meaning drift"
    },
    {
      "command": "git show 8cda46da:<file> for pre-epic comparison",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "Verified 12 pre-epic rule texts against current HEAD equivalents"
    }
  ],
  "validationOutput": [
    "39 rules sampled across 11 batches",
    "Zero meaning drift in any sampled rule",
    "All modality changes (lowercase must/do not → MUST/MUST NOT) are RFC-2119 formalization of existing obligation",
    "One genuine semantic addition: internal_tooling_direct_gate (new state, not a rewrite)",
    "Redundant-text removal class: deduplication via cross-references; normative content preserved at owner location"
  ],
  "residualRisks": [
    "Non-sampled rules not spot-checked (~60 additional rules in required-rules.json); sampling coverage is ~40% of the 100+ rule IDs. Pattern consistency across all sampled batches suggests low risk of hidden drift, but a full exhaustive audit would cover the remaining 60%."
  ],
  "noStagedFiles": true,
  "diffSummary": "Audit output only. No source changes.",
  "reviewFindings": [
    "No blockers. Pattern is consistent: prose → rule-ID mechanical transformation with RFC-2119 formalization. The only non-mechanical change (internal_tooling_direct_gate) is explicitly additive."
  ],
  "manualNotes": "The 11-batch epic + post-epic changes follow a single coherent pattern. The transformation is best understood as a structural refactoring (making rules addressable) rather than a semantic revision. Every sampled before/after pair confirms this pattern holds across all document families."
}
```

